      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Moisture content can absolutely affect walnut's brittleness; wood that is too dry becomes prone to cracking and splintering along the grain lines where the tool pushes. Before trying different stones, I recommend flattening your piece by flowing damp paste or applying a wet cloth during cutting to soften the critical fibers at the tips. Once the grains are lubricated by moisture, your sharp chisels will slice more cleanly rather than tearing the brittle material.",
